yeah, sure.

00:29:22.232 --> 00:29:23.940
So what you've developed
here essentially

00:29:23.940 --> 00:29:28.320
acts as a wrapper on top of,
let's say, [INAUDIBLE],, or GBM.

00:29:28.320 --> 00:29:31.670
So why is it not more generic
to any other, like CAD Boost

00:29:31.670 --> 00:29:32.500
or Random Forest?

00:29:32.500 --> 00:29:35.730
Why do you limit it to
XGBoost or Lite GBM?

00:29:35.730 --> 00:29:38.464
KARTHIK RAMASAMY: So for
single node training, you can--

00:29:41.007 --> 00:29:43.090
For single node training,
that's a great question,

00:29:43.090 --> 00:29:46.250
but a good observation.

00:29:46.250 --> 00:29:47.760
Yeah.

00:29:47.760 --> 00:29:51.690
If I were to paraphrase the
question, what I've shown here,

00:29:51.690 --> 00:29:52.740
it seems like a generic.

00:29:52.740 --> 00:29:53.240
Right?

00:29:53.240 --> 00:29:54.840
Like you are executing
a Python file,

00:29:54.840 --> 00:29:57.298
