00:53:25.030 --> 00:53:29.990
But there's one more
project called meta--

00:53:29.990 --> 00:53:35.970
Let me kind of show you that.

00:53:35.970 --> 00:53:40.630
So we've been saying
this is a big issue.

00:53:40.630 --> 00:53:41.130
Right?

00:53:41.130 --> 00:53:42.750
When people train
multiple models,

00:53:42.750 --> 00:53:46.020
they want to kind of track
and analyze hyperparameters

00:53:46.020 --> 00:53:47.360
and [INAUDIBLE] models, right?

00:53:47.360 --> 00:53:51.030
So this Kubeflow metadata is
another component of Kubeflow

00:53:51.030 --> 00:53:54.210
that's useful to capture the
metadata about your training

00:53:54.210 --> 00:53:59.340
job, like how many layers did
you use, where is your model,

00:53:59.340 --> 00:54:00.635
how much accuracy you got?

00:54:00.635 --> 00:54:02.010
And finally, you're
able to bring

00:54:02.010 --> 00:54:04.850
back to your notebook
[INAUDIBLE] Panda's dataframe

00:54:04.850 --> 00:54:06.190
and you're able to analyze that.

00:54:06.190 --> 00:54:10.890
So this is like a much
more earlier stage.

00:54:10.890 --> 00:54:14.230
But you will probably
keep watching this.

00:54:14.230 --> 00:54:17.570
You will hear back soon.

00:54:17.570 --> 00:54:19.570
AUDIENCE: If I want to
get profiling information

00:54:19.570 --> 00:54:23.490
and [INAUDIBLE] so that if
